# Training and analysis

Live steepwell sweep (tmux `steepwell_invariant`, 60M epochs, `MAX_PARALLEL_JOBS=3` on cuda:0):

`milestones/fcn2_erf_hidden_kernel/red_robin_alpha_beta_invariant_steepwell_a01_g1.25_P0160_betamax100_nu0.25_N01000_sa00.03_ens1_Asnap_eps0.5_lr0.01_ep60M_sched2_3_5/`

Five β points; red-robin. `A_snapshots/` are written only **after** the 60M schedule (then 2M extra, interval 20k). Until then use `model.pt` / `checkpoint.pt`.

Snapshot files: `A_snapshots/epoch_*.pt` with `{epoch, A, W0}`. Pool `W0[:,:,0]` for posterior histograms.

Best existing posterior for bimodality: `red_robin_d50_T0.2_P3000_N400_chi400_eps0.5_lr0.01_ep50M_weight_snaps/` (late Langevin, ~196 snaps).

VGA CLI: `julia julia_lib/fcn2_vga_erf.jl --d --n1 --P --chi --kappa --epsilon --s0 --sa0 --to out.json`. **Default is the matrix Laplace saddle.** `--laplace-mean` gives σ=0, `--linear` drops He1–He3 coupling, and `--vga` (or `--offdiag`/`--advanced`/`--regularized`) selects the old variational solver; `--vga --matrix` is matrix VGA. For sigma_a runs you **must** pass `--sa0` (`plot_action_h0_activation.py` does). Laplace modes scan a μ₀×σ₀ grid, accept residual < 1e-5, keep the largest μ.

Overlays: `plot_action_h0_activation.py --group <G> [--vga-laplace|--vga-laplace-mean] [--vga-matrix]` → `<G>_vga_laplace[_mean][_matrix]/`. Always κ_eff (default); never `--vga-bare-kappa` unless asked. σ=0 theory is drawn as ±μ vertical lines.

`μ=0` is always a VGA stationary point. `fcn2_vga_erf.jl` default μ₀=0.1 collapses the whole steepwell ray except d=50 onto that saddle (lWT still looks fine). For this ray, scan μ₀∈{0.25,…,0.50} as in `plot_invariant_vga_actions_alpha_scale.jl`; all five points are then bimodal with μ≈0.36–0.41.
